@startuml activity-consult-first
!include _style.iuml
title Activity — inspection on request / customisation (UC05, UC06, UC31, UC07)

|Customer|
|Service advisor|
|System|
|Customer|
start
:Choose "Check something specific"
or "Customise my vehicle";
:Pick the vehicle and the areas,
describe it in own words, pick a dealership;
:Send to an advisor;
|System|
:Store the request: **SUBMITTED**,
log consultation.submitted;
|Service advisor|
:Open the "Waiting for advice" queue;
:Read the areas and the description;
if (Can the workshop do it?) then (no)
  :Decline with a message to the customer;
  |System|
  :**REJECTED**;
  |Customer|
  :Read the advisor's reason;
  stop
else (yes)
  |Service advisor|
  :Set time needed, skill, bay type,
  estimate and a message, then approve;
  note right
    The server checks the bay type fits the vehicle
    and the skill exists; if not → 422 and the
    advisor corrects it.
  end note
  |System|
  :**APPROVED**, log consultation.reviewed;
endif
|Customer|
:See the reply on Home and on Requests
(duration, estimate, advisor's note);
if (Book it?) then (withdraw)
  |System|
  :**CANCELLED**;
  stop
else (pick a time)
  repeat
    |Customer|
    :Pick a start time — only times with a bay of the
    approved type and a technician with the approved skill;
    |System|
  repeat while (Still APPROVED and the slot still free?) is (slot taken: offer alternatives)
  -> yes;
  note right
    Already booked by another tab or device
    → 409 CONSULTATION_NOT_BOOKABLE
  end note
  :In one transaction: appointment **HELD** for 10 minutes,
  request **BOOKED**;
  |Customer|
  :Review and press **Confirm booking**;
  |System|
  if (Confirmed before the hold ran out?) then (yes)
    :HELD → **CONFIRMED**;
  else (no)
    :HELD → **EXPIRED**,
    request back to **APPROVED**
    so another time can be picked;
    stop
  endif
endif
|Customer|
if (Cancels before the start?) then (yes)
  |System|
  :Appointment CANCELLED,
  request back to **APPROVED**
  so another time can be picked;
else (no)
endif
stop
@enduml
